## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of practical, beginner-friendly schema evolution across HTTP input, DB writes, and Kafka events without breaking existing consumers.

## Key Concepts

- Backward-compatible schema evolution
- Optional/additive fields and defaults
- Schema registry with compatibility levels
- Canary rollout and feature flags
- Contract and end-to-end testing

## Code Example

```javascript
const Ajv = require("ajv");
const ajv = new Ajv();
const schema = {
  type: "object",
  properties: {
    id: { type: "string" },
    event: { type: "string" },
    customer_segment: { type: "string" }
  },
  required: ["id", "event"],
  additionalProperties: true
};
function validate(payload){
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, payload);
  if(!valid) throw new Error(ajv.errors.map(e=>e.message).join(", "));
  return payload;
}
```

